        "start_line": 538,
        "end_line": 542,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "performance",
        "title": "Per-packet IOVA->VA translation no longer compiled out for PHYS_IOVA builds",
        "explanation": "The removed call sites wrapped this prefetch in #ifndef RTE_LIBRTE_DPAA2_USE_PHYS_IOVA because in physical-IOVA mode DPAA2_IOVA_TO_VADDR is a table/memseg lookup rather than a cast. The new helper is called unconditionally (except on LX2160A) for every dequeued frame in dpaa2_dev_prefetch_rx, dpaa2_dev_rx and dpaa2_dev_tx_conf, so PHYS_IOVA builds now pay a costly translation per packet just to issue a prefetch hint, often on a not-yet-valid next DQ entry.",
        "suggestion": "Restore the #ifndef RTE_LIBRTE_DPAA2_USE_PHYS_IOVA guard inside dpaa2_dev_prefetch_next_psr (making it a no-op in PHYS_IOVA mode) or at its call sites.",
        "evidence": "\tannotation = DPAA2_IOVA_TO_VADDR(annot_iova);",
        "confidence": 0.55,
